        "note.002.source.end" "43"
        "note.003.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.003.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.001.text" "Additional current paths bypass this binding table: captured mouse motion supplies"
        "note.003.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.002.text" "[look (locator=look)](controls.dsl) through `orbit_camera.gd`; native panel ItemLists supply"
        "note.003.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.003.text" "[ui-navigate (locator=ui-navigate)](controls.dsl), [ui-select (locator=ui-select)](controls.dsl) and"
        "note.003.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.004.text" "[ui-activate (locator=ui-activate)](controls.dsl), including pointer double-activation. Their precise native"
        "note.003.line.005.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.005.text" "physical event defaults are not a selected portable profile. Activation dispatches"
        "note.003.line.006.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.006.text" "[equip-item (locator=equip-item)](controls.dsl), [use-inventory-item (locator=use-inventory-item)](controls.dsl),"
        "note.003.line.007.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.007.text" "[spend-skill-point (locator=spend-skill-point)](controls.dsl), [buy-item (locator=buy-item)](controls.dsl) or"
        "note.003.line.008.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.008.text" "[sell-item (locator=sell-item)](controls.dsl) by list context. Inventory consumable activation uses the"
        "note.003.line.009.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.009.text" "selected bag item, unlike `quick-item`'s current first-consumable-stack target."
        "note.003.source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "note.003.source.start" "45"
        "note.003.source.end" "53"
        "note.004.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.004.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.004.line.001.text" "**Shared-input boundaries:** current NPC dispatch checks an NPC before a ground item; this is"
        "note.004.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.004.line.002.text" "an implementation observation, not a new general priority rule for pickup/climb/objects/pets."
        "note.004.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.004.line.003.text" "Multiple panels independently own cursor state; no exclusive context stack or global priority"
        "note.004.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.004.line.004.text" "is selected here. Inventory/skills/shop retain current input restrictions and"
        "note.004.line.005.state" "text"
        "note.004.line.005.text" "[live time (locator=hud-element)](3_Classes.dsl). `menu`/shop cancellation must not be mistaken for one"
        "note.004.line.006.state" "text"
        "note.004.line.006.text" "canonical meaning or a decision to pause. The alias `ultimate` cannot create another skill."
        "note.004.source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "note.004.source.start" "55"
        "note.004.source.end" "60"
        "note.005.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.005.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.005.line.001.text" "No executable mappings exist for separate block, swimming ascent, mount/dismount, glider/boat,"
        "note.005.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.005.line.002.text" "object activation, formula learning, quick cycling or bench/map manipulation."
        "note.005.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.005.line.003.text" "[Map operations (locator=screens-and-contextual-ui)](controls.dsl) have unselected physical gestures;"
        "note.005.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.005.line.004.text" "obsolete source maps are not defaults. No extra inventory alias, standing dodge alias, class chord or"
        "note.005.line.005.state" "text"
        "note.005.line.005.text" "UI-scale binding is inherited. Rebinding UI/persistence and device-resolved prompts are deferred."
        "note.005.source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "note.005.source.start" "62"
        "note.005.source.end" "66"
    }
}

r_c_gamepad = element "c-gamepad" "SectionNote" {
    tags "SectionNote,Overview"
    properties {
        "id" "c-gamepad"
        "kind" "SectionNote"
        "order" "68"
        "source.commit" "175e0c59b6a05ead62d29bd851085cd5a3818378"
        "source.status" "historical baseline coordinates"
        "source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "source.start" "68"
        "source.end" "75"
        "title" "Gamepad"
        "heading.level" "2"
        "heading.slug" "gamepad"
        "section" "Overview"
        "note.001.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.001.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.001.text" "Stable profile ID: `gamepad`. **Unselected / unimplemented.** Refers to every applicable"
        "note.001.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.002.text" "[canonical action](controls.dsl), including separate movement/look, block/special, jump/ascent,"
        "note.001.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.003.text" "interaction/pickup/climb, recall/mount, slots and contextual UI/map operations. Buttons, axes,"
        "note.001.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.004.text" "triggers, layout, focus navigation, sensitivity/deadzones and shared-input shapes have not been"
        "note.001.line.005.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.005.text" "chosen. Native UI support alone is not a gameplay profile; do not inherit keyboard coupling."
        "note.001.source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "note.001.source.start" "70"
        "note.001.source.end" "74"
    }
}

r_c_android = element "c-android" "SectionNote" {
    tags "SectionNote,Overview"
    properties {
        "id" "c-android"
        "kind" "SectionNote"
        "order" "76"
        "source.commit" "175e0c59b6a05ead62d29bd851085cd5a3818378"
        "source.status" "historical baseline coordinates"
        "source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "source.start" "76"
        "source.end" "89"
        "title" "Android"
        "heading.level" "2"
        "heading.slug" "android"
        "section" "Overview"
        "note.001.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.001.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.001.text" "Stable profile ID: `android`. **FIRST-SLICE RUNTIME / OWNER HARDWARE-TESTED.** The"
        "note.001.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.002.text" "[selected native Godot stack](../decisions/android-native-touch-controls.md) is `VirtualJoystick`,"
        "note.001.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.003.text" "`TouchScreenButton` and a dedicated touch-look region. The physical policy below"
        "note.001.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.004.text" "serves the same [54-action catalog](controls.dsl),"
        "note.001.line.005.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.005.text" "not a reduced or reinterpreted scheme. Widgets do not implement the catalog or decouple consumers."
        "note.001.line.006.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.006.text" "The first-slice native adapter and separated consumers have desktop synthetic regressions and"
        "note.001.line.007.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.007.text" "windowed visual checks, and the owner has tested the game on Android hardware. Device/OS details,"
        "note.001.line.008.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.008.text" "individual acceptance-check coverage and render-cost measurements are not recorded; this is not a"
        "note.001.line.009.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.009.text" "claim that every checklist item was verified. The full catalog and broader implementation remain"
        "note.001.line.010.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.010.text" "deferred. Unmapped features gain no physical defaults."
        "note.001.source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "note.001.source.start" "78"
        "note.001.source.end" "87"
        "note.002.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.002.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.001.text" "<a id=\"android-layout\"></a>"
        "note.002.anchor.001" "android-layout"
        "note.002.source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "note.002.source.start" "89"
        "note.002.source.end" "89"
    }
}

r_c_landscape_layout_and_fixed_joystick = element "c-landscape-layout-and-fixed-joystick" "SectionNote" {
    tags "SectionNote,Overview"
    properties {
        "id" "c-landscape-layout-and-fixed-joystick"
        "kind" "SectionNote"
        "order" "90"
        "source.commit" "175e0c59b6a05ead62d29bd851085cd5a3818378"
        "source.status" "historical baseline coordinates"
        "source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "source.start" "90"
        "source.end" "97"
        "title" "Landscape layout and fixed joystick"
        "heading.level" "3"
        "heading.slug" "landscape-layout-and-fixed-joystick"
        "section" "Overview"
        "note.001.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.001.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.001.text" "Landscape in either direction; a fixed movement joystick at bottom-left, a right-side drag"
        "note.001.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.002.text" "region for look, and separate action buttons. Keep controls within the screen safe area and"
        "note.001.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.003.text" "each touch target at least 48 dp wide and high. Block and special have separate buttons;"
        "note.001.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.004.text" "NPC Talk and Pick Up remain separate. No automatic targeting or lock-on is introduced."
        "note.001.source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "note.001.source.start" "92"
        "note.001.source.end" "95"
        "note.002.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.002.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.001.text" "<a id=\"android-response\"></a>"
        "note.002.anchor.001" "android-response"
        "note.002.source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "note.002.source.start" "97"
        "note.002.source.end" "97"
    }
}

r_c_movement_response_and_camera_sensitivity = element "c-movement-response-and-camera-sensitivity" "SectionNote" {
    tags "SectionNote,Overview"
    properties {
        "id" "c-movement-response-and-camera-sensitivity"
        "kind" "SectionNote"
        "order" "98"
        "source.commit" "175e0c59b6a05ead62d29bd851085cd5a3818378"
        "source.status" "historical baseline coordinates"
        "source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "source.start" "98"
        "source.end" "112"
        "title" "Movement response and camera sensitivity"
        "heading.level" "3"
        "heading.slug" "movement-response-and-camera-sensitivity"
        "section" "Overview"
        "note.001.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.001.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.001.text" "For joystick radius R, displacement of magnitude <= 0.15 R requests neutral. Beyond that,"
        "note.001.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.002.text" "normalize the direction and request the existing full walking/swimming speed; retain existing"
        "note.001.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.003.text" "movement eligibility, multipliers and costs from `generators.json#design.movement`."
        "note.001.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.004.text" "Sprint is a separate hold: no automatic sprint or new slow-walk curve."
        "note.001.source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "note.001.source.start" "100"
        "note.001.source.end" "103"
        "note.002.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.002.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.001.text" "Dragging right looks right; dragging up looks up. Let W be the usable safe-area screen width"
        "note.002.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.002.text" "and dx/dy the right/down-positive screen deltas in the same units. Apply yaw adjustment"
        "note.002.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.003.text" "`-180 degrees * dx / W` and pitch adjustment `-180 degrees * dy / W`: a full-width drag turns"
        "note.002.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.004.text" "180 degrees, with the same degrees-per-distance vertically. Preserve existing"
        "note.002.line.005.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.005.text" "`generators.json#design.camera.pitch-deg` bounds; add no acceleration. This is Android-only"
        "note.002.line.006.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.006.text" "response, not a change to mouse sensitivity or a selection of saved settings."
        "note.002.source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "note.002.source.start" "105"
        "note.002.source.end" "110"
        "note.003.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.003.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.001.text" "<a id=\"android-finger-ownership\"></a>"
        "note.003.anchor.001" "android-finger-ownership"
        "note.003.source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "note.003.source.start" "112"
        "note.003.source.end" "112"
    }
}

r_c_finger_ownership_and_simultaneous_controls = element "c-finger-ownership-and-simultaneous-controls" "SectionNote" {
    tags "SectionNote,Overview"
    properties {
        "id" "c-finger-ownership-and-simultaneous-controls"
        "kind" "SectionNote"
        "order" "113"
        "source.commit" "175e0c59b6a05ead62d29bd851085cd5a3818378"
        "source.status" "historical baseline coordinates"
        "source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "source.start" "113"
        "source.end" "124"
        "title" "Finger ownership and simultaneous controls"
        "heading.level" "3"
        "heading.slug" "finger-ownership-and-simultaneous-controls"
        "section" "Overview"
        "note.001.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.001.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.001.text" "Each physical touch owns the control where it starts until release/cancellation. Movement"
        "note.001.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.002.text" "and look each accept one owner; action buttons accept independent fingers. Crossing another"
        "note.001.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.003.text" "control never activates it. Extra fingers on an occupied control do nothing and cannot take"
        "note.001.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.004.text" "over when its owner leaves. No captured or ignored touch transfers to another control;"
        "note.001.line.005.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.005.text" "activation requires a fresh touch."
        "note.001.source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "note.001.source.start" "115"
        "note.001.source.end" "119"
        "note.002.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.002.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.001.text" "Movement, look and an action must work simultaneously, without overriding gameplay eligibility"
        "note.002.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.002.text" "or costs. A touch must never also generate a duplicate mouse-driven action."
        "note.002.source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "note.002.source.start" "121"
        "note.002.source.end" "122"
        "note.003.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.003.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.001.text" "<a id=\"android-interruption\"></a>"
        "note.003.anchor.001" "android-interruption"
        "note.003.source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "note.003.source.start" "124"
        "note.003.source.end" "124"
    }
}

r_c_intentional_release_versus_interruption = element "c-intentional-release-versus-interruption" "SectionNote" {
    tags "SectionNote,Overview"
    properties {
        "id" "c-intentional-release-versus-interruption"
        "kind" "SectionNote"
        "order" "125"
        "source.commit" "175e0c59b6a05ead62d29bd851085cd5a3818378"
        "source.status" "historical baseline coordinates"
        "source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "source.start" "125"
        "source.end" "140"
        "title" "Intentional release versus interruption"
        "heading.level" "3"
        "heading.slug" "intentional-release-versus-interruption"
        "section" "Overview"
        "note.001.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.001.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.001.text" "For [charged specials (locator=special-attack)](3_Classes.dsl), only a normal release by the owning finger"
        "note.001.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.002.text" "inside the special button intentionally completes the charge under existing execution rules."
        "note.001.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.003.text" "Sliding outside cancels without firing or spending reserved MP; interruption never becomes"
        "note.001.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.004.text" "release-to-fire. Cancellation adds no MP refund beyond not spending the reserved amount."
        "note.001.line.005.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.005.text" "Instant specials retain their trigger shape."
        "note.001.source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "note.001.source.start" "127"
        "note.001.source.end" "131"
        "note.002.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.002.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.001.text" "For held buttons, sliding outside ends the request; sliding back does not restart it. The same"
        "note.002.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.002.text" "physical touch cannot rearm or transfer: a fresh touch is required. Focus loss, backgrounding,"
        "note.002.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.003.text" "panel opening, layout changes and death clear outstanding touch requests and cancel unfinished"
        "note.002.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.004.text" "charges. Returning never resumes them automatically. Already-fired attacks, running abilities"
        "note.002.line.005.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.005.text" "and cooldowns retain their existing rules; committed effects are not undone. This selects input"
        "note.002.line.006.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.006.text" "cleanup, not background simulation, pause or save policy."
        "note.002.source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "note.002.source.start" "133"
        "note.002.source.end" "138"
        "note.003.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.003.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.001.text" "<a id=\"android-panels\"></a>"
        "note.003.anchor.001" "android-panels"
        "note.003.source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "note.003.source.start" "140"
        "note.003.source.end" "140"
    }
}

r_c_inventory_skills_and_shop_touch_interaction = element "c-inventory-skills-and-shop-touch-interaction" "SectionNote" {
    tags "SectionNote,Overview"
    properties {
        "id" "c-inventory-skills-and-shop-touch-interaction"
        "kind" "SectionNote"
        "order" "141"
        "source.commit" "175e0c59b6a05ead62d29bd851085cd5a3818378"
        "source.status" "historical baseline coordinates"
        "source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "source.start" "141"
        "source.end" "154"
        "title" "Inventory, skills and shop touch interaction"
        "heading.level" "3"
        "heading.slug" "inventory-skills-and-shop-touch-interaction"
        "section" "Overview"
        "note.001.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.001.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.001.text" "One inventory, skills or shop panel owns the screen at a time; opening another replaces it"
        "note.001.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.002.text" "without leaking gameplay input. Gameplay touch controls, including look, are unavailable"
        "note.001.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.003.text" "while browsing. [Time still runs and players remain vulnerable (locator=hud-element)](3_Classes.dsl)."
        "note.001.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.004.text" "Panel transitions clear outstanding touches under the [interruption rule (locator=android-interruption)](controller-profiles.dsl)."
        "note.001.source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "note.001.source.start" "143"
        "note.001.source.end" "146"
        "note.002.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.002.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.001.text" "Tap a row to select it, then use a clearly labeled **Equip / Use / Spend / Buy / Sell** button"
        "note.002.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.002.text" "for the corresponding existing operation. Scrolling or selecting alone never commits an"
        "note.002.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.003.text" "operation; confirmation commits only on release inside its button. Close or Android Back"
        "note.002.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.004.text" "closes the panel and consumes that input; gameplay requires fresh touches afterward."
        "note.002.line.005.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.005.text" "This selects no other menu or keyboard behavior."
        "note.002.source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "note.002.source.start" "148"
        "note.002.source.end" "152"
        "note.003.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.003.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.001.text" "<a id=\"android-first-slice\"></a>"
        "note.003.anchor.001" "android-first-slice"
        "note.003.source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "note.003.source.start" "154"
        "note.003.source.end" "154"
    }
}

r_c_first_implementation_scope_and_button_activation = element "c-first-implementation-scope-and-button-activation" "SectionNote" {
    tags "SectionNote,Overview"
    properties {
        "id" "c-first-implementation-scope-and-button-activation"
        "kind" "SectionNote"
        "order" "155"
        "source.commit" "175e0c59b6a05ead62d29bd851085cd5a3818378"
        "source.status" "historical baseline coordinates"
        "source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "source.start" "155"
        "source.end" "170"
        "title" "First implementation scope and button activation"
        "heading.level" "3"
        "heading.slug" "first-implementation-scope-and-button-activation"
        "section" "Overview"
        "note.001.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.001.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.001.text" "The first separately authorized implementation adapts currently working gameplay: movement"
        "note.001.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.002.text" "and look, sprint, separate Jump / Swim Up, basic/special attacks, block, dodge, available class"
        "note.001.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.003.text" "slots, separate Talk / Pick Up, Quick Item, inventory, skills, shops and camera zoom. These"
        "note.001.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.004.text" "map to the existing distinct [canonical actions](controls.dsl), not new gameplay permissions."
        "note.001.line.005.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.005.text" "Gameplay trigger buttons fire once on touch-down, without repetition; held and charged actions"
        "note.001.line.006.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.006.text" "retain their own lifecycles. [Panel confirmations (locator=android-panels)](controller-profiles.dsl) commit on release inside."
        "note.001.line.007.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.007.text" "Entering a new context never converts an existing hold into another action."
        "note.001.source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "note.001.source.start" "157"
        "note.001.source.end" "163"
        "note.002.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.002.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.001.text" "Keep the current first-consumable-stack Quick Item approximation for this slice, not as the"
        "note.002.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.002.text" "final consumable-selection or channel policy. Unimplemented climbing, pets, gliding, crafting"
        "note.002.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.003.text" "and map features remain deferred, not removed from the 54-action target. Adapting working"
        "note.002.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.004.text" "features does not authorize implementing missing gameplay."
        "note.002.source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "note.002.source.start" "165"
        "note.002.source.end" "168"
        "note.003.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.003.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.001.text" "<a id=\"android-request-order\"></a>"
        "note.003.anchor.001" "android-request-order"
        "note.003.source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "note.003.source.start" "170"
        "note.003.source.end" "170"
    }
}

r_c_requests_arriving_together = element "c-requests-arriving-together" "SectionNote" {
    tags "SectionNote,Overview"
    properties {
        "id" "c-requests-arriving-together"
        "kind" "SectionNote"
        "order" "171"
        "source.commit" "175e0c59b6a05ead62d29bd851085cd5a3818378"
        "source.status" "historical baseline coordinates"
        "source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "source.start" "171"
        "source.end" "179"
        "title" "Requests arriving together"
        "heading.level" "3"
        "heading.slug" "requests-arriving-together"
        "section" "Overview"
        "note.001.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.001.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.001.text" "Interruptions and UI ownership first suppress uncommitted gameplay requests. Otherwise apply"
        "note.001.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.002.text" "current movement/look and held defence updates, then process action requests in arrival order."
        "note.001.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.003.text" "After each request, check existing eligibility, resources and cooldowns for the next. This is"
        "note.001.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.004.text" "adapter ordering, not a new exclusive-one-action rule or additional attack permission."
        "note.001.line.005.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.005.text" "No automatic retries or buffered attacks; already-committed effects are not undone."
        "note.001.source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "note.001.source.start" "173"
        "note.001.source.end" "177"
        "note.002.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.002.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.001.text" "<a id=\"android-camera-zoom\"></a>"
        "note.002.anchor.001" "android-camera-zoom"
        "note.002.source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "note.002.source.start" "179"
        "note.002.source.end" "179"
    }
}

r_c_camera_zoom_mapping = element "c-camera-zoom-mapping" "SectionNote" {
    tags "SectionNote,Overview"
    properties {
        "id" "c-camera-zoom-mapping"
        "kind" "SectionNote"
        "order" "180"
        "source.commit" "175e0c59b6a05ead62d29bd851085cd5a3818378"
        "source.status" "historical baseline coordinates"
        "source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "source.start" "180"
        "source.end" "188"
        "title" "Camera zoom mapping"
        "heading.level" "3"
        "heading.slug" "camera-zoom-mapping"
        "section" "Overview"
        "note.001.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.001.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.001.text" "Separate **Camera nearer / Camera farther** buttons map to [zoom (locator=zoom)](controls.dsl). Each tap"
        "note.001.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.002.text" "applies one existing `generators.json#design.camera.distance.step` toward nearer/farther within"
        "note.001.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.003.text" "the existing minimum/maximum bounds; no held repetition or pinch gesture. Distance zero"
        "note.001.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.004.text" "retains first-person view. Finger ownership, panel gating and trigger rules above apply;"
        "note.001.line.005.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.005.text" "map zoom is distinct and remains deferred."
        "note.001.source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "note.001.source.start" "182"
        "note.001.source.end" "186"
        "note.002.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.002.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.001.text" "<a id=\"android-device-scope\"></a>"
        "note.002.anchor.001" "android-device-scope"
        "note.002.source.file" "controller-profiles.md"
        "note.002.source.start" "188"
        "note.002.source.end" "188"
    }
}

r_c_device_switching_and_customization_in_this_slice = element "c-device-switching-and-customization-in-this-slice" "SectionNote" {
    tags "SectionNote,Overview"
    properties {
        "id" "c-device-switching-and-customization-in-this-slice"
        "kind" "SectionNote"
        "order" "189"
